{"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"BrazeKit"}],"title":"Device ID Configuration"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Configuring your user’s device ID with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Customize-Behavior","title":"Customize Behavior","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class","doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/BrazeDelegate","doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/overrideResourceBundle"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BrazeKit"},{"type":"text","text":", a user can be identified using one of two device ID options:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/uidevice\/1620059-identifierforvendor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" property.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A randomly generated UUID.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"text":" may not be available in all scenarios or devices, Braze provides the option to use a more generic UUID to identify a user’s device.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The below configuration (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","type":"reference"},{"text":") is deprecated and will be removed in a future major release. After removal, the SDK will always use a randomly generated UUID as the device ID. Device IDs previously persisted from the ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifierForVendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" continue to be respected until local persistence is cleared, at which point the device moves to a UUID-based device ID.","type":"text"}]}]},{"text":"Setting Your Configuration","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Setting-Your-Configuration"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To configure this option, set ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" under ","type":"text"},{"code":"Braze.Configuration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Assigning this property to ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will generate a random UUID for each user installation, whereas a value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will notify the SDK to use the device’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"identifierForVendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let configuration = Braze.Configuration(","    apiKey: \"<BRAZE_API_KEY>\",","    endpoint: \"<BRAZE_ENDPOINT>\"",")","\/\/ Set this value to `true` to opt out of `identifierForVendor` usage.","configuration.useUUIDAsDeviceId = true","let braze = Braze(configuration: configuration)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Starting in 7.0.0, the default value for this property is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For device types that do not support "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":", such as watchOS or macOS, Braze will default to a randomly generated UUID regardless of which option is configured."}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After being generated, device IDs created from UUIDs will remain consistent throughout the lifetime of the application’s installation or until "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/wipeData()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is called."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Since calling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/wipeData()"},{"text":" will erase all local SDK storage, the device ID that was previously stored will be deleted. Thus, if ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId"},{"text":" is enabled, the SDK will generate a new UUID for the device ID after this operation. Similarly, if ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Braze\/documentation\/BrazeKit\/Braze\/Configuration-swift.class\/useUUIDAsDeviceId"},{"text":" is disabled, the SDK will re-use the same IDFV after this operation.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Migrating from a Previous Version","anchor":"Migrating-from-a-Previous-Version","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are migrating your project from the legacy "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Appboy\/appboy-ios-sdk","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or from a version of the Braze Swift SDK prior to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5.7.0"},{"type":"text","text":", note that the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifierForVendor"},{"type":"text","text":" op